# C++ namespaces (two public layers + `detail`)

Public C++ namespaces stop at **two** levels. Anything deeper uses the **hybrid** rule below.

Applies to **new** trees (`core/`, `src/` new modules, `algorithm/`). Legacy `branches/` code keeps existing `Smt_*` namespaces.

## Shape

| Layer | Role | Examples |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1–2 | **Public** API / module identity | `core`, `core::math`, `geo`, `ui::views`, `render::skia` |
| 3 | **`detail` only** (internals) | `core::detail`, `geo::detail`, `ui::views::detail` |

## Hybrid placement

- **Public / semi-public** symbols that today sit in a third semantic namespace (`::flow`, `::core`, `::builder`, `::runtime`, …) ? **hoist** to `area::module`. On name collisions, rename the type/function (keep the two-layer namespace).
- **Internal** symbols (`*detail*`, `draft`, `test`, `example`, `demo`, `benchmark`, nested helpers) ? `area::module::detail`. Do **not** keep names like `webui_detail` / `parallel_detail` as the third namespace segment; merge into `detail`.
- Directory layout (`src/ui/views/…`) does **not** justify a third named public namespace.

## Do

- **Do** use at most **`area::module`** for symbols callers are meant to name.
- **Do** put non-exported helpers, codecs, and file-local building blocks in **`…::detail`** (or an anonymous namespace in a `.cpp`).
- **Do** apply this to **new or touched** translation units; when editing a file that already has a third semantic namespace, **fold it into the two-layer parent or into `detail`** in the same change when practical.

## Don’t

- **Don’t** introduce a third (or deeper) **semantic** namespace such as `core::math::vector` or `geo::algorithm::buffer` for public or semi-public types.
- **Don’t** nest further named layers under `detail` for taxonomy (`…::detail::codec::v1`); keep `detail` flat and distinguish with **type/file names**.
- **Don’t** treat this rule as applying to **mojom `module`**, protobuf `package`, Python modules, or Win32 namespaces.

## Examples

```cpp
// BAD — third semantic layer
namespace geo {
namespace algorithm {
namespace buffer {
struct Options { /* ... */ };
}
}
}

// GOOD — public type at two layers
namespace geo {
struct BufferOptions { /* ... */ };
}

// GOOD — internal helper under detail
namespace geo {
namespace detail {
inline bool decode_buffer_options(const std::string& wire, BufferOptions* out);
}
}
```

